# Storyteller, incidents, quests, research, stats (P2-02, P2-03, P2-14).

@class RimStorytellerInfo
def: string Def name of the storyteller
label?: string Name shown to the player
difficulty?: string Difficulty name
threat_points?: number Points the storyteller would use for a threat on the current map right now
wealth?: number Colony wealth the storyteller sees
colonists?: integer Colonists the storyteller counts

@class RimStorytellerDef
def: string Def name of the storyteller
label?: string Name shown to the player
visible: boolean Whether the player can pick it

@class RimIncidentDef
def: string Def name of the incident
label?: string Name shown to the player
category?: string Category it is listed under
base_chance: number Base chance of being picked
min_threat_points: number Fewest threat points it needs
pointless: boolean Whether threat points do not matter

@class RimIncidentOptions
points?: number Threat points
faction?: RimFaction Faction that sends it
forced?: boolean Fire even when the game says it cannot

@class RimQuestInfo
id: integer Id of the quest, to pass back to the functions that take one
name?: string Quest name
state: string NotYetAccepted, Ongoing, EndedSuccess, EndedFailed, EndedOfferExpired, EndedUnknownOutcome or EndedInvalid
root?: string Quest script def name
challenge: number Challenge rating
age_ticks: integer How many ticks old it is
accepted: boolean Whether the player accepted it
hidden: boolean Whether it is hidden
parts: integer How many parts it has

@class RimResearchInfo
def: string Def name of the research
label?: string Name shown to the player
cost: number Research points needed
progress: number Research points done
progress_pct: number 0 to 1
finished: boolean Whether it is finished
can_start: boolean Whether it can be researched now
tab?: string Research tab def name
tech_level: string Tech level name, for example Industrial
prerequisites: string[] Project defs needed first
techprints: integer Techprints needed
techprints_applied: integer Techprints applied

@class RimKnowledge
project?: string Current project def name
progress: number Progress on it

@class RimStatExplanation
value: number The stat value
text: string Line by line breakdown, as the game shows it
final: string The value formatted as the game shows it

@class RimStatDef
def: string Def name of the stat
label?: string Name shown to the player
category?: string Category it is listed under
show: boolean Whether the stat is shown to the player

@kit domain=storyteller op=storyteller subject=none title="Storyteller" page=storyteller
info() -> RimStorytellerInfo | The storyteller, difficulty, threat points, wealth and colonists.
defs() -> RimStorytellerDef[] | Every storyteller def.
set(def: string) -> string | Switches the storyteller. Returns the def name.
threat_points(map?: RimMapRef) -> number | Threat points for a map, the current map by default.
difficulty() -> table<string, number|boolean> | Every numeric and boolean difficulty setting.
set_difficulty(name: string, value: number|boolean) -> string | Changes one difficulty setting, for example threatScale.

@kit domain=incidents op=incident subject=none title="Incidents" page=storyteller
defs() -> RimIncidentDef[] | Every incident def with category and chance.
can_fire(def: string, opts?: RimIncidentOptions, h?: RimMapRef) -> boolean | Whether the game would let the incident fire now.
fire(def: string, opts?: RimIncidentOptions, h?: RimMapRef) -> boolean | Fires an incident with options on a map (the current map by default).
queue(def: string, ticks: integer, opts?: RimIncidentOptions, h?: RimMapRef) -> boolean | Queues an incident to fire after some ticks.

@kit domain=quests op=quest subject=none title="Quests" page=storyteller
list(state?: string) -> RimQuestInfo[] | Every quest, optionally only those in one state.
defs() -> string[] | Every quest script def name.
generate(root: string, points?: number) -> RimQuestInfo | Generates a quest from a script and makes it available.
accept(id: integer, pawn?: RimPawn) -> boolean | Accepts a quest offer.
finish(id: integer, outcome?: string) -> string | Ends a quest with Success, Fail, InvalidPreAcceptance or Unknown. Returns the new state.
signal(tag: string) -> boolean | Sends a quest signal that quest parts listen for.
slate_get(name: string) -> any | A value of the quest slate while a Lua quest node runs, such as points, map, asker or any value an earlier node stored. nil when it is not set.
slate_set(name: string, value: any, kind?: string) -> boolean | Stores a number, string or boolean in the quest slate for later nodes. kind forces int, float, string or bool, because slate values are typed.
slate_set_object(name: string, target: RimObject) -> boolean | Stores a game object (a pawn, thing, map or faction) in the quest slate.

@kit domain=research op=research subject=none title="Research" page=research
list(filter?: string) -> RimResearchInfo[] | All projects, or only finished, available or locked ones.
info(def: string) -> RimResearchInfo | One project.
current() -> RimResearchInfo? | The project being researched.
set_current(def: string) -> boolean | Starts researching a project.
finish(def: string) -> boolean | Completes a project at once, with the game's letter.
set_progress(def: string, progress: number) -> number | Sets the progress of a project, clamped to its cost.
knowledge(category: string, add?: number) -> RimKnowledge | Anomaly knowledge. Adds points to a category (Basic or Advanced) when asked.

@kit domain=stats op=stat subject=thing:RimThingRef title="Stats" page=research
value(stat: string) -> number? | The final value of a stat for a thing, nil when the stat is disabled for it.
explain(stat: string) -> RimStatExplanation | The value with the game's own explanation of where it comes from.

@kit domain=stats op=stat subject=none title="Stats" page=research
defs(category?: string) -> RimStatDef[] | Every stat def, optionally one category.
